%% As-built pipeline, superseding the original pre-implementation sequence diagram
%% (git history: HEAD~ of this file, the .NET/Chroma/Opus Writer design).
%% Every Note below states what was designed vs what shipped, and why it changed.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant CC as Claude Code
    participant Shim as hook/shim.py<br/>(UserPromptSubmit)
    participant Daemon as daemon/server.py<br/>Daemon (resident, one per machine)
    participant DB as SQLite index<br/>(FTS5 + sqlite-vec, one file per repo)
    participant Ranker as rank/ LightGBM reranker
    participant Rg as ripgrep fallback

    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)
        Note over CC, Rg: DEVIATION - the original diagram had a Harness calling a separate<br/>cloud WriterModel (Opus) plus a SilentVerifier that compiled the diff.<br/>Neither exists. Claude Code is both the caller and the writer, there is<br/>no second model in this repo, no compile-and-repair loop, no cloud call.
    end

    %% ========== STAGE 0: INDEX MAINTENANCE (OFF THE REQUEST PATH) ==========
    Note over Daemon, DB: DEVIATION - designed as a Hook-triggered diff_and_refresh against<br/>Chroma, run synchronously per prompt (Stage 0 of the original diagram).<br/>Shipped as a continuous background watcher (index/RepoWatcher, 1s debounce)<br/>that never sits on the request path. Freshness key is xxhash3-128 of<br/>WORKING-TREE CONTENT, not a git hash, because the files an agent is<br/>mid-edit on are uncommitted, and those are exactly the ones retrieval<br/>must not be stale on. Changed files are re-chunked with tree-sitter at<br/>symbol granularity, FTS5 rows and import-graph edges rebuilt, dense<br/>vectors marked pending for the async backfill loop (Daemon._backfill_loop).

    %% ========== STAGE 1: THE HOOK ==========
    User ->> CC: types a prompt
    CC ->> Shim: UserPromptSubmit (JSON on stdin)
    activate Shim
    Note over Shim: DEVIATION - designed as an HTTP POST to a Harness process.<br/>Shipped as a stdlib-only, dependency-free CLI shim (hook/shim.py)<br/>invoked as a subprocess. Import cost is user-visible latency on every<br/>prompt, so nothing beyond the standard library loads here. All real<br/>work happens in the resident daemon over a Unix socket.

    Shim ->> Daemon: op retrieve, repo, prompt, assemble false<br/>over daemon.sock, 3s timeout (HYBRID_RETRIEVAL_TIMEOUT)
    activate Daemon
    alt daemon unreachable
        Daemon --x Shim: connection refused or timeout
        Shim ->> Shim: autostart(), spawn hybrid-retrieval serve detached, exit 0
        Note over Shim: This prompt gets nothing, the next one will.<br/>Fails open, always. Any error, timeout, missing daemon or unindexed<br/>repo results in exit 0 with no injected context (ground rule in CLAUDE.md).
    end

    %% ========== STAGE 2: SKIP RULE ==========
    Note over Daemon: skip.should_skip(prompt, cfg.skip), fires before any retrieval work.<br/>Patterns, then meta-questions, then usable query terms after stopword<br/>removal (min 2). A skipped prompt still returns a result (skipped equals<br/>reason), did nothing and never ran must not look identical in the trace.

    %% ========== STAGE 3: CANDIDATE GENERATION ==========
    par Sparse (always) - retrieve/sparse.py
        Daemon ->> DB: FTS5 BM25, top 80 (cfg.retrieval.sparse_k)
        DB -->> Daemon: sparse candidates
    and Dense (only when the loaded model matches the index) - retrieve/dense.py
        Daemon ->> DB: int8 KNN top 200 (rescore_k), then float32 rescore
        Note over DB: DEVIATION - designed against Chroma with a 768-dim vector and a<br/>separate query_dense call. Shipped as sqlite-vec in the SAME database<br/>file as FTS5 (dense_is_ready in retrieve/pipeline.py checks the index's<br/>recorded model id and dim against the loaded embedder, a mismatch just<br/>skips dense rather than erroring). No ANN index exists in sqlite-vec, so<br/>the int8 scan is linear and float32 rescore restores precision on the survivors.
        DB -->> Daemon: dense candidates
    end

    %% ========== STAGE 4: FUSION ==========
    Daemon ->> Daemon: rrf_fuse(dense, sparse, k=60), cut to 50 (fuse_to)
    Note over Daemon: DEVIATION - designed as union two 100-lists, take top 100, with an<br/>AST-boosted sparse stage (import traversal, depth 2, always on).<br/>Shipped as RRF fusion cut to 50, and AST expansion defaults OFF<br/>(cfg.retrieval.ast_depth = 0), measured neutral-to-negative versus BM25<br/>alone. The import graph is still built and still feeds the reranker as<br/>in/out-degree features, only the candidate-expansion use stopped.

    %% ========== STAGE 5: RERANK (replaces the local Scorer tier) ==========
    Daemon ->> Ranker: rerank(candidates, 22 features) - rank/features.py + rank/gate.py
    activate Ranker
    Note over Ranker: DEVIATION - designed as a fine-tuned quantized 3B LoRA model doing 100<br/>forward passes per prompt, prompt plus file text into a logit.<br/>Shipped as a LightGBM lambdarank model over structured features (dense<br/>and sparse scores and ranks, RRF, matching chunks, AST degree, path-token<br/>overlap, symbol exact match, file size, is_test, is_generated, is_doc,<br/>is_config, is_script, point-in-time git recency and churn). A missing or<br/>unloadable ranker is not fatal, retrieve() leaves the fused RRF order in<br/>place (Daemon._state loads it once per repo and logs, never raises).<br/>Trained on real prompts mined from agent session history, not commit messages.
    Ranker -->> Daemon: reranked order plus GateDecision
    deactivate Ranker

    %% ========== STAGE 6: CONFIDENCE GATE + FALLBACK ==========
    Note over Daemon: DEVIATION - designed as softmax over 100 logits with max_prob above<br/>0.85 and margin above 0.15 over a temperature-scaled distribution,<br/>judging the single best file. Shipped as rank/gate.evaluate(): judges<br/>the SET, the trained ranker's top_score against min_top_score, and the<br/>margin between the last-selected and first-rejected candidate against<br/>min_boundary_margin. Both thresholds are calibrated on held-out data<br/>(gate.calibrate) and stored in the model artefact, not guessed.

    alt HIGH confidence
        Daemon ->> Daemon: selected equals ordered top_n (default 5)
    else LOW confidence
        Daemon ->> Rg: ripgrep_candidates(repo_root, prompt, allowed indexed paths)
        Note over Rg: Same idea as the original diagram's targeted grep and cat, but it<br/>REPLACES the ranking wholesale (decision 28) rather than being a<br/>separate verification pass, and only ripgrep is used, never plain grep,<br/>so it respects .gitignore and skips binaries. It is also literally the<br/>function the benchmark's B0 arm calls, what the pipeline falls back to<br/>and what it must beat are the same implementation.
        Rg -->> Daemon: ranked paths
    end

    %% ========== STAGE 7: ASSEMBLY / RENDER, now paths-only ==========
    Note over Daemon: DEVIATION (most recent, SPEC 10j, decision 29 reversed by measurement)<br/>- the original assemble_slim_context built a roughly 3.8k-token bundle<br/>of full file contents plus AST subtree plus a hardcoded dependency<br/>manifest, sent to the Writer. retrieve/pipeline.py still CAN assemble<br/>full content (tiered, small file whole with comments stripped, large<br/>file imports plus signatures only) but only when a caller asks for it,<br/>the CLI query command and the dashboard probe endpoint do. The hook<br/>passes assemble false, assembling the top 5 of this repo for one prompt<br/>measured about 19,600 tokens against a roughly 2,095 token break-even,<br/>and hook output above roughly 40KB gets spilled by the harness to a<br/>file the agent then spends turns reading. So the request that matters<br/>most gets NO file contents from the daemon at all.

    Daemon ->> DB: trace.record(prompt, result, session_id), writes traces table
    Daemon -->> Shim: ok, paths, tokens, dense_used, reranked,<br/>fell_back, skipped, gate, trace_id, latency_ms, stage_ms
    deactivate Daemon

    Shim ->> Shim: render(paths) builds a retrieved-context block,<br/>numbered path list only, no file contents (hook/shim.py)
    Note over Shim: HEADER is explicit about weight, a ranked guess not a constraint,<br/>open what looks useful and ignore the rest. Paths cost roughly 2% of<br/>full-content assembly and still remove the search, the agent opens<br/>named files instead of grepping for them.
    Shim -->> CC: hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext (or nothing, exit 0)
    deactivate Shim
    CC ->> User: response, with the ranked files already named in context

    %% ========== ADDED, NOT IN THE ORIGINAL DESIGN AT ALL ==========
    rect rgb(255, 248, 240)
        Note over Daemon: NEW COMPONENT, no equivalent in the original design, a local HTTP<br/>dashboard (dashboard/server.py plus api.py) for inspecting index status,<br/>per-repo config overrides, trace history, and a manual probe that runs<br/>retrieve() with full assembly and shows every stage's contribution<br/>(dense, sparse, fuse, rerank, gate). Off the request path entirely,<br/>started via the dashboard CLI command, not wired into UserPromptSubmit.
    end
